WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.270 position:50% size:92% align:center
The eight tokens choose four categories. The

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:06.061 position:50% size:92% align:center
counts tell us the size of each output region.

00:00:06.281 --> 00:00:09.187 position:50% size:92% align:center
They do not by themselves say where each token

00:00:09.187 --> 00:00:11.145 position:50% size:92% align:center
ID belongs within its category.

00:00:13.165 --> 00:00:15.817 position:50% size:92% align:center
The count kernel finishes before the route

00:00:15.817 --> 00:00:18.783 position:50% size:92% align:center
kernel begins in the same stream. Device-memory

00:00:18.783 --> 00:00:20.488 position:50% size:92% align:center
counts therefore supply the

00:00:20.488 --> 00:00:22.381 position:50% size:92% align:center
region sizes before placement.

00:00:22.601 --> 00:00:25.581 position:50% size:92% align:center
Exclusive category starts identify where each

00:00:25.581 --> 00:00:27.700 position:50% size:92% align:center
category’s output region begins.

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:32.914 position:50% size:92% align:center
Token five belongs to category zero. Two earlier

00:00:32.914 --> 00:00:35.110 position:50% size:92% align:center
tokens have that category, so its

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:36.973 position:50% size:92% align:center
within-category rank is two.

00:00:37.193 --> 00:00:39.613 position:50% size:92% align:center
The route kernel’s completed shared prefix

00:00:39.613 --> 00:00:41.341 position:50% size:92% align:center
stages supply this rank before

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:42.377 position:50% size:92% align:center
the scatter write.

00:00:44.397 --> 00:00:46.692 position:50% size:92% align:center
A category’s start plus the token’s

00:00:46.692 --> 00:00:49.772 position:50% size:92% align:center
earlier-match rank gives the destination. Token

00:00:49.772 --> 00:00:52.525 position:50% size:92% align:center
five therefore writes output position two.

00:00:52.745 --> 00:00:56.293 position:50% size:92% align:center
The SM performs this address calculation; GPU

00:00:56.293 --> 00:00:58.894 position:50% size:92% align:center
memory holds the category regions

00:00:58.894 --> 00:01:01.023 position:50% size:92% align:center
and their stored token IDs.

00:01:03.043 --> 00:01:06.032 position:50% size:92% align:center
Token seven also belongs to category zero.

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:08.950 position:50% size:92% align:center
Suppose its write is inspected before the

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:10.872 position:50% size:92% align:center
other category-zero writes.

00:01:11.092 --> 00:01:13.505 position:50% size:92% align:center
Pause and predict whether it should take

00:01:13.505 --> 00:01:15.857 position:50% size:92% align:center
position zero or retain the destination

00:01:15.857 --> 00:01:18.089 position:50% size:92% align:center
determined by its earlier-match rank.

00:01:23.909 --> 00:01:26.789 position:50% size:92% align:center
Token seven has three earlier matching tokens,

00:01:26.789 --> 00:01:29.042 position:50% size:92% align:center
so it retains position three even if

00:01:29.042 --> 00:01:30.544 position:50% size:92% align:center
its write happens first.

00:01:30.764 --> 00:01:33.803 position:50% size:92% align:center
Atomic arrival tickets can make updates unique

00:01:33.803 --> 00:01:36.908 position:50% size:92% align:center
without preserving input order. Stable grouping

00:01:36.908 --> 00:01:39.617 position:50% size:92% align:center
needs the explicit prefix rank used here.

00:01:41.637 --> 00:01:44.494 position:50% size:92% align:center
The completed grouping places zero, two, five

00:01:44.494 --> 00:01:47.414 position:50% size:92% align:center
and seven in the first region, followed by one

00:01:47.414 --> 00:01:49.381 position:50% size:92% align:center
and four, then three, then six.

00:01:49.601 --> 00:01:52.442 position:50% size:92% align:center
Choose the required output contract first:

00:01:52.442 --> 00:01:55.147 position:50% size:92% align:center
counts need safe additions; stable token

00:01:55.147 --> 00:01:57.379 position:50% size:92% align:center
grouping also needs ordered ranks

00:01:57.379 --> 00:01:59.137 position:50% size:92% align:center
and distinct destinations.
